From bd1a67dc644cdf69e4b190abf5fc19e734a82531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:03:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Show a stored filename as text where it enters the
 minibuffer

TAB in the buffer and search prompts and completion cycling put a buffer's name
into the minibuffer raw, so invalid UTF-8 could reach a row, and from there be
yanked into a file buffer.  A line feed split the prompt across rows.  The name
now goes through the existing sanitiser, a line feed showing as ^J.  It's just
text from then on, and doesn't refer to the original.

File matches are unchanged: scanDir filtered the name, and the rest was typed.

The error for a file that can't be opened at startup printed the name and message
raw to the terminal; it now sanitises both.

Stored paths stay raw: opening, editing and saving use the real path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01947MBgCkoERXfoyRGfCmQi
